cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OASR in your research or product, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "OASR: Open Automatic Speech Recognition"
abstract: >-
  OASR is a high-performance CUDA inference and serving engine for automatic
  speech recognition. It serves seven encoder architectures (Conformer,
  Zipformer, RNN-T, FastConformer, Whisper, Paraformer and Qwen2-Audio) across
  five decode paradigms (CTC, transducer, attention encoder-decoder,
  non-autoregressive CIF and speech-LLM) from one engine, with custom
  CUDA/CUTLASS kernels, GPU CTC and WFST beam search, offline and streaming
  recognition, W8A8 int8/fp8 quantization, and a Rust front-end exposing an
  OpenAI-compatible HTTP API, a realtime WebSocket and gRPC.
authors:
  - family-names: Dang
    given-names: Bao Chien
repository-code: "https://github.com/chiendb97/oasr"
url: "https://github.com/chiendb97/oasr"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - automatic speech recognition
  - speech-to-text
  - inference engine
  - model serving
  - CUDA
  - streaming ASR
  - Whisper
  - Conformer
  - Zipformer
  - RNN-T
  - Paraformer
  - speech LLM
